{"id":"815bab30f29d1caf","group":"58","path":"58/batch15/58-thm-open-mapping.md","title":"Open Mapping Theorem","display":"thm-open-mapping — Open Mapping Theorem","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-open-mapping","aliases":["58-thm-open-mapping"],"display":"thm-open-mapping — Open Mapping Theorem","depends_on":["[[../batch05/58-df-banach-space.md]]","[[../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md]]","[[../batch05/58-df-surjective.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-open-mapping"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-open-mapping</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-open-mapping — Open Mapping Theorem"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"ef59807ad934771f\" href=\"?note=ef59807ad934771f\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-banach-space.md\">../batch05/58-df-banach-space.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"261de7e0269cd7e2\" href=\"?note=261de7e0269cd7e2\" title=\"../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md\">../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"9f8cb046321ba311\" href=\"?note=9f8cb046321ba311\" title=\"../batch05/58-df-surjective.md\">../batch05/58-df-surjective.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"X,Y,K,+_X,\\odot_X,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y\\in V\">\\(X,Y,K,+_X,\\odot_X,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y\\in V\\)</span> are two normed-space structures over the same scalar field <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"K\">\\(K\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"T\\in{}^X Y\">\\(T\\in{}^X Y\\)</span>.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Banach}_S(-,K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|)\">\\(\\mathrm{Banach}_S(-,K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|)\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Surjective}\">\\(\\mathrm{Surjective}\\)</span> are the exact structured predicates from the dependencies.</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}open-mapping}\\vdash{}\n&amp;\\mathrm{Banach}_S(X,K,+_X,\\odot_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\n\\land\\mathrm{Banach}_S(Y,K,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S\n(T,X,Y,K,+_X,\\odot_X,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\n\\land\\mathrm{Surjective}(T,X,Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in Y\\;\n\\bigl(\\|y\\|_Y&lt;r\\to\n\\exists x\\in X\\;(\\|x\\|_X&lt;1\\land T(x)=y)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}open-mapping}\\vdash{}\n&amp;\\mathrm{Banach}_S(X,K,+_X,\\odot_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\n\\land\\mathrm{Banach}_S(Y,K,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S\n(T,X,Y,K,+_X,\\odot_X,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\n\\land\\mathrm{Surjective}(T,X,Y)\\\\\n&amp;\\to\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{&gt;0}\\;\\forall y\\in Y\\;\n\\bigl(\\|y\\|_Y&lt;r\\to\n\\exists x\\in X\\;(\\|x\\|_X&lt;1\\land T(x)=y)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>The displayed norms are now the same norms used by both Banach predicates and by bounded linearity. The conclusion says that the image of their open unit ball contains an open ball about <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"0\">\\(0\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>It follows from Baire category theorem.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch05/58-df-banach-space.md","status":"resolved","id":"ef59807ad934771f","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-banach-space.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md","status":"resolved","id":"261de7e0269cd7e2","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch02/58-df-bounded-linear.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch05/58-df-surjective.md","status":"resolved","id":"9f8cb046321ba311","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch05/58-df-surjective.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"X,Y,K,+_X,\\odot_X,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y\\in V","display":false},{"tex":"K","display":false},{"tex":"T\\in{}^X Y","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Banach}_S(-,K,+,\\odot,\\|\\cdot\\|)","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{Surjective}","display":false},{"tex":"\\begin{aligned}\n\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}open-mapping}\\vdash{}\n&\\mathrm{Banach}_S(X,K,+_X,\\odot_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_X)\n\\land\\mathrm{Banach}_S(Y,K,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\\\\\n&\\land\\mathrm{BoundedLinear}_S\n(T,X,Y,K,+_X,\\odot_X,+_Y,\\odot_Y,\\|\\cdot\\|_X,\\|\\cdot\\|_Y)\n\\land\\mathrm{Surjective}(T,X,Y)\\\\\n&\\to\\exists r\\in\\mathbb R_{>0}\\;\\forall y\\in Y\\;\n\\bigl(\\|y\\|_Y<r\\to\n\\exists x\\in X\\;(\\|x\\|_X<1\\land T(x)=y)\\bigr).\n\\end{aligned}","display":true},{"tex":"0","display":false}],"bytes":1377,"backlinks":[{"id":"84daad544872cc71","anchor":"ref-4333","locations":["正文"],"count":1,"excerpt":"[[../batch15/58-thm-open-mapping.md|58-thm-open-mapping]]（batch15）"}],"outgoing":["ef59807ad934771f","261de7e0269cd7e2","9f8cb046321ba311"]}